  "content": {
    "body": "The graph works in BOTH directions: spec can lead code (forward) or be\nrecovered from code (reverse). Statuses carry the truth either way.\n\n## Forward: spec → code\n\n1. /pebbles-plan decomposes a requirement into verifiable pieces —\n   checklist items with testable descriptions, linked pebbles (workflow,\n   models) connected via refs. Everything starts `planned`.\n2. Implementation (via /pebbles-fix or the implement intent) makes code\n   satisfy the spec; statuses move to `implemented` per touched unit.\n3. /pebbles-verify holds spec against reality: locate the implementation\n   (codeLinks first, then the map), compare actual behavior to the\n   claim, set TRUTHFUL statuses at both levels, and record the result\n   as a finding — verified-working with proof, or bug/spec-violation.\n4. /pebbles-audit sweeps for rot on a schedule: fresh map, then every\n   implemented/verified pebble's codeLinks re-checked — file gone →\n   `missing`, symbol gone → `drift`, behavior broken → `broken` —\n   each with a finding.\n\n## Reverse: code → spec (the code is the source of truth)\n\n- /pebbles-extract fills ONE pebble from the real implementation.\n  Sequence: map (--fresh if stale) → locate via map-symbol/map-search →\n  read the actual source → update with FULL content: models get real\n  fields (type, required = NOT NULL, primaryKey, refKey for every FK\n  whose target model exists, default, description from code context),\n  workflows get the real flow, apis the real endpoints → link-code\n  every source file → status implemented per unit (verified only if\n  behavior was proven).\n- /pebbles-onboard onboards an ENTIRE existing app: map --fresh →\n  inventory the domain from hubs (most-imported files ARE the core) →\n  batch-create models/structures/apis/workflows with real content,\n  linked and code-linked → report progress per batch and what remains.\n\n## Findings: the append-only evidence log\n\nFindings are DATED reports (createdAt is the report date), cross-linked\nboth ways to what they judge — never hand-crafted. They cover\nEVERYTHING with an outcome: failures (bug · spec-violation · security ·\nperformance · regression · tech-debt · ux · data), pass evidence\n(verified-working), and knowledge outcomes (research · decision ·\nassumption · measurement · incomplete).\n\nAPPEND-ONLY: never update or delete a finding. Same question with a\nnew answer → NEW finding with --supersedes linking the old one (which\nstays untouched); a new question → fresh finding. Disposition is set\nat birth and immutable — open (needs action) · resolved (settled) ·\ninfo (no action implied). \"Is it still open?\" = walk the supersedes\nchain: the latest entry wins; superseded findings are history.\n\nMANDATORY findings: verify, audit, fix, implement, investigate, impact\nand coverage runs end with at least one finding — even \"inconclusive\"\nis an outcome; a run with no recorded outcome is unauditable.\nextract/onboard/sync-model/plan file one only when something notable\nsurfaced; read/query work never (retrieval is not an outcome). Audits\nre-confirm stale open chain-tips by appending the current truth, so\nthe log can't rot into phantom open bugs. A finding without evidence\nis an opinion. /pebbles-report digests chain-TIPS newest-first,\nflagging aged open tips as unconfirmed.\n\n## Analysis toolkit\n\n- /pebbles-coverage: gaps in both directions — spec without codeLinks,\n  hub code without spec, requirements without test refs.\n- /pebbles-impact: blast radius before a change — spec dependents (refs\n  + backlinks) plus code importers (map-neighbors --in) and callers\n  (map-callers), ranked by importedBy.\n- query --status / --unit-status: the work queue — what's planned,\n  what's broken, at pebble or unit granularity.",
    "kind": "text"
  },
  "createdAt": "2026-07-21T14:32:38.669Z",
  "description": "The full working loops: forward (plan→implement→verify→audit), reverse (extract/onboard), findings as evidence, and the analysis toolkit.",
